So it's about much more than about particular interests of Men Medau," says Pötzl.
Whether the criticism of the parent advisory board of the crèche, with the expansion of the road, one "of the few natural spots of Coburg would be lost", "can be decided by the reader himself".
At the beginning of October, Pötzl, together with the Bamberg State Construction Office, intends to inform the city councils about the structural development of the university until 2020 "and in this context address the significance of the new development".
Peer Medau had informed the parents of the nursery last week about the plans of the university.
Accordingly, the access for the new parking deck should lead not as before via the campus and Friedrich-Streib-Straße, but over the Medau mountain.
Thus, the narrow road would have to be upgraded over a length of about one kilometre in two lanes.
According to Medaus projections, the traffic in the park of Hohenfels Castle would increase tenfold.
There is talk of about 2000 vehicles per day.
On the part of the city, they did not want to comment on the project so far.
Glandorf resigns from handball national team
Holger Glandorf will no longer play for the DHB team.
The 31-year-old from Bundesliga side SG Flensburg-Handewitt cited mainly health problems for this decision.
The decision was not easy for me, it has matured over several months.
It's time for me to listen to the signals of my body and end my career in the national team," the 2007 world champion shared on his Facebook page.
He thus retires with a record of 167 international matches and 576 goals for Germany.
Because the powerful backroom player for the Champions League winner from Flensburg wants to chease goals for a few more years, he is no longer available to the new national coach Dagur Sigurdsson.
Glandorf had a "long and good conversation" with the Icelander, who will announce his squad for the international matches against Switzerland on Tuesday.
His ideas and approaches inspired me just as much as my long-time teammates and my successors will inspire me.
But for my club, I would also like to be healthy in the next few years, but longer regeneration breaks are necessary, which the current double burden does not allow.
The left-hander even had to fear his career end in 2012 after a heel infection.
Due to Achilles tendon problems, he had been treated by team doctors of the German Handball Federation (DHB) with a cortisone syringe, which later triggered severe inflammation.
An emergency operation and two other interventions followed.
Then Glandorf had announced a lawsuit against the team doctor, the altercation ended with a settlement.
Twelve-years of professional and eleven years of national team career do not pass without a trace on any body.
I've got some health construction sites that I can't ignore anymore.
After the three infection-related foot surgeries, which took place at short intervals in 2012, I never really got my blood pressure under control.
There are some other wear-related complaints.
Already at the beginning of the year I realized that although I can control my head, I cannot deceive my bodie, Glandorf explained in an interview to the magazine "Handball Time".
For a comeback, he'd only be ready in an absolute emergency.
"When all the ropes break, I'm always ready to talk," the two-time family man explained to the trade magazine.
However, I can count the years in which I can still play handball on one hand.
I also have to say that, after my long hospital stay in 2012, I have also become quite humilious about my health.
After my career, I want to be able to go, at least,
In addition to the 2007 World Cup title and winning the Champions League in 2014, he won the EHF Cup in 2008 (HSG Nordhorn) and 2010 (TBV Lemgo).
In 2012 he also secured the European Cup Winners’ Cup with Flensburg.
German economy shrunk by 0.2 percent in spring
Crises around the globe have slowed the German economy in the second quarter.
Gross domestic product fell 0.2 per cent from April to the end of June 2014 compared with the previous quarter.
This was announced by the Federal Statistical Office and thus confirmed preliminary calculations.
Consumption alone revived the economy in the spring, while investment declined.
Foreign trade also put the brakes on the economy.
Thanks to the strong start to the year, there is an overall GDP increase of 0.8 percent for the first half of 2013 compared to the second half of 2013.
Horstmar was the starting point and the destination of the "Münsterland-Mooiste", which led for the first time throught through Burgmannsstadt on Sunday.
Horstmar's Burgmann town experienced an invasion of Dutch "Fietzenfahrer" on Sunday.
The largest cycling association in the Netherlands, NTFU, organized the so-called "Münsterlande-Mooiste".
This is the biggest bike tour across Münsterland, the cyclist paradise near the Netherlands.
More than 1000 participants thanked Jos ter Huerne for organising this tour through Münsterland.
This tour was advertised in various trade journals.
We're from Den Helder and went overnight to take part in this tour.
