TWO youthful bushiers were airlifted to safety with the winch after being trapped in the Blue Mountains in NSW throughout the night.
THE 16-year-old girl and 19-year-old man embarked on their tour shortly after Sunday noon in Govett's Leap in Blackheath.
Concerned relatives called police at about 8 p.m. when the two had not returned home.
A search squad from local police and ambulance services broke open and the pair were found at about 3pm near the Bridal Veil waterfalls.
